  "slug": "learning-quantum-1f91",
  "summary": "Four November 2026 preprints assess photonic and quantum learning hardware through simulation, functional evaluation, hybrid circuits, and qubit tuning.",
  "synthesis": "All four items are preprints linking learning architectures to physically grounded hardware models, the dominant thread being that device physics and functional performance are evaluated together. PISim couples DNN workloads with physics-based models of photonic accelerators, modulators, and laser sources for cross-layer design-space exploration. A separate proposal evaluates optical neural network modules against performance-matched digital replacements using an expressivity-based, function-oriented methodology. On the quantum side, hybrid PointNet-quantum networks with five QFT circuit configurations are assessed for LiDAR classification, while an FPGA-in-the-loop gradient descent system autonomously tunes spin qubits in electrostatically defined quantum dots. The novelty lies in closed-loop, hardware-aware assessment of learning systems; the available summaries report no quantitative comparisons across these approaches.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-24"
}
